    "created_at": "2016-01-15T23:39:24Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-15T23:39:24Z",
    "body": "I think these kind of nonlocal patches are not great; implementers forget them when implementing a function just from its spec section. Instead each of the three methods should be modified to add a sentence of this sort.\n\nIs the goal here that other places in the spec that create ImageData do not rethrow the error? E.g. structured clone? If so, here would be my proposal:\n- Add a paragraph after the \"New ImageData objects must be initialised...\" paragraph saying \"Creation of the new Canvas Pixel ArrayBuffer may fail, per the JavaScript specification's definition for how to create an ArrayBuffer. By default, this must be ignored (???? what happens then???), but in some cases an algorithm that creates a new ImageData object will specify to <dfn>rethrow any ImageData creation exceptions</dfn>, in which case the caller must rethrow any exceptions encountered while creating the ArrayBuffer. [ECMA262]\"\n- Update the three call sites to add a \"<span>Rethrow any ImageData creation exceptions</span>.\" sentence.\n\nIf the intention was that all call sites should rethrow, then:\n- Add a note (instead of the above suggested normative paragraph): \"Creation of the new Canvas Pixel ArrayBuffer may fail, per the JavaScript specification's definition for how to create an ArrayBuffer. Algorithms which create a new ImageData object will rethrow such exceptions. [ECMA262]\"\n- Update all call sites to say \"Rethrow any exceptions encountered while creating the new ImageData object.\"\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
