    "created_at": "2016-01-18T09:10:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-18T09:10:28Z",
    "body": "1. Even though IDL says that, we are usually explicit about exceptions in specifications that build on top of IDL. In part because the exceptions sometimes have to go elsewhere.\n2. I think the proper way to fix this would be by defining the allocation of `ImageData` objects. And then, reference that from its constructor, `createImageData()`, etc.\n3. Even if IDL points out that the buffer associated with the view can not always be allocated, we'll still need to handle that exception.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
