    "created_at": "2016-01-18T16:21:07Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-01-18T16:21:48Z",
    "body": "Okay, defining the allocation of ImageData objects, then referencing it in all the appropriate places sounds reasonable to me. That pattern is found throughout the spec, and it is one that I have often appreciated as an implementer.  \n\nAlso, I can add the reference to [ECMA262], but I think that should be as a note, and that the normative text should remain orthogonal (i.e. language-neutral) by using a generic reference to \"the scripting language's specification\". Is that correct?\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
