    "body": "> Also, I can add the reference to [ECMA262], but I think that should be as a note, and that the normative text should remain orthogonal (i.e. language-neutral) by using a generic reference to \"the scripting language's specification\". Is that correct?\n\nNo, it is not. The spec is no longer language-neutral; we expunged that fantasy. IDL bindings exist for JS, and ArrayBuffer objects are created according to the JS specification.\n",
